+## Independent property symmetry
+
+`WANNIER90%SYMMETRY T` optionally reduces the scalar and second-variational SOC diagonalizations for
+`KPOINTS_SOURCE NNKP`, `WILSON`, `TRIM` and `SYMMETRY`. This is independent of the SCF mesh:
+
+```text
+&WANNIER90
+  KPOINTS_SOURCE WILSON
+  SOC T
+  SYMMETRY T
+  SYMMETRY_BACKEND SPGLIB
+  EPS_SYMMETRY 1.0E-6
+  EPS_SYMMETRY_OPERATORS 1.0E-8
+&END WANNIER90
+```
+
+Symmetry is off by default; `SYMMETRY_BACKEND` defaults to `K290` and also accepts `SPGLIB` in a
+build with that library. A restricted SCF is required. The property point set need not be closed
+under the crystal point group: a Wilson half-plane generally is not. The internal property-only
+orbit mode relates points present in the requested set, without adding missing integration points.
+The ordinary `KPOINTS%SCHEME GENERAL` closure requirement is unchanged. Repeated reciprocal images
+are deduplicated for diagonalization only, not in the Wilson graph.
+
+At each representative the scalar eigenproblem is solved once. The cell-Fourier-gauge AO action
+includes the atom permutation, real-spherical basis rotation and the image phase
+$\exp(-2\pi i\mathbf k_t\cdot\mathbf L_A)$. Complex conjugation is included for an antiunitary
+operation. Every reconstructed scalar frame is checked against the actual target $S(\mathbf k)$ and
+$H(\mathbf k)$, including both $HC-SC\varepsilon$ and its MO projection. The latter checks energy
+errors that can be amplified by an ill-conditioned AO basis. There is no target Ritz diagonalization
+or silent full-mesh fallback. A symmetry-broken frozen potential therefore cannot be accepted just
+because the nuclear geometry has the requested symmetry.
+
+SOC is diagonalized only at the same representatives. Since the scalar target gauge was generated
+with a known AO action, its second-variational spinor coefficients can be transformed with the
+corresponding conjugate SU(2) representation and physical time reversal. CP2K uses the conjugate
+spin representation because its SOC assembly convention is $(\sigma_x,-\sigma_y,\sigma_z)$. The
+complete reconstructed SOC eigenframe is checked for normalization and its target Hamiltonian
+residual before selecting exported bands. A scalar SOC window ending inside a degenerate manifold is
+rejected; increase `WANNIER90%ADDED_MOS`. The size of this window must still be converged for
+physical results.
+
+All ordered cross-k AO overlaps, band weights, Wilson directions and reciprocal boundary shifts
+remain those of the full requested calculation. Thus arbitrary unitary gauges inside degenerate
+spaces cancel between adjacent links; equality of individual MO coefficients or raw `.mmn` entries
